d Images Marketing & Communication Media Services Missions & Chaplain Services PUC Church Records SERVE - Survivor Empowerment, Response to Violence, and Education Service Learning Student Finance Student & Spiritual Life Student Success Center Student Wellness Center | Counseling Services Student Wellness Center | Health Services Title IX Community Recreation Contact Career Center Pacific Union College Lower Level Education Building One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Phone: (707) 965-7085 Email: career@puc.edu Career Center Choosing a career is like piecing together a puzzle. Input from family and friends, interest and personality inventories, paid and volunteer life experiences and prayer are integral components in finding a career about which you feel passionate. PUC has various resources available to assist you in your search for a career- including this career planning guide to give you ideas and keep you on track each year. 4-year Career Planning Guide Our Career Counselor is available to help you clarify your interests, strengths, and values- as well as provide valuable information about various majors and career options. If you have questions about your options or don't know what to major in, make an appointment to talk with our counselor and begin your career exploration process. Career Information Salary.com This site gives salary information based on location. Career One Stop ( www.careeronestop.org ) You can browse different careers, watch videos, and compare jobs by state. \n  There is also information on resumes, interviews, networking, and more. Occupation Information Network ( www.online.onetcenter.org ) One of the largest career information resources, this site also allows you to search jobs titles by skills, personality, and industry. Road Trip Nation ( www.roadtripnation.com ) Ever wonder how people get the job they have? They will personally tell you about their career path on this site. Watch fun, informational interviews made by students like you. Salary Calculator by State ( http://goodcalculators.com/salary-calculator ) We help you to understand the average salary in the US for \ndifferent industries with our handy salary calculator. Internships Internships  are a great way to explore working in a certain field. Many internship opportunities are available directly through the major academic departments and through checking with the Career & Counseling Center. Monster College A wide variety of postings made available only to participating colleges. Choose \"Search Jobs & Internships\"; then find PUC under \"college and university career centers.\" Type \"PUC\" in the password box if necessary, then hit the search box next to \"monster.com entry-level search\" at the bottom of the page. Contact Career Center Pacific Union College Lower Level Education Building One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Phone: (707) 965-7085 Email: career@puc.edu Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Campus Map (800) 862-7080 (707) 965-6313 Apply Give Contact Visit Careers Academics Useful Links Information Academic Departments Bookstore Calendar Campus Map Consumer Information Directory Disability Services Discrimination Policy Emergency Info Library News Online Programs Pay Student Bill Photo Gallery Privacy Policy PUC CARES Act Grant Records Office Student Planning Title IX Information For Who Are You? Current Students New Students Future Students Transfer Students Parents & Families Alumni Visitors Faculty & Staff Veterans © Copyright 2026. Pacific Union College. All Rights reserved. | Privacy policy"
