ervices Missions & Chaplain Services PUC Church Records SERVE - Survivor Empowerment, Response to Violence, and Education Service Learning Student Finance Student & Spiritual Life Student Success Center Student Wellness Center | Counseling Services Student Wellness Center | Health Services Title IX Community Recreation Contact Us Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Phone: (707) 965-6231 Fax: (707) 965-6400 hr@puc.edu Employee Benefits Program Full, Assistant, or Associate Professor of Communication Applications are available in the Human Resources Office or available online . Applications from current employees are welcome. Applicants must be members of the Seventh-day Adventist Church. Email ( hr@puc.edu ), fax (707-965-6400), or mail (Human Resources Office, One Angwin Avenue, Angwin, CA 94508), your signed application to Human Resources Please contact Human Resources regarding questions about this position. Applications from qualified applicants are forwarded to the employing department by Human Resources Applicants selected for interviews will be contacted by Human Resources or the employing department Apply for job Start Date Upon receipt of qualified applicant Job Type Faculty Job Opening Department Arts, Humanities and Professions Position Type Part-time Tenure Track Yes Job Summary The part-time Faculty Member in Communication is responsible for providing high-quality instruction in assigned communication courses and supporting student learning and academic success. The position teaches courses as assigned, maintains effective communication with students, assesses student performance, and contributes to a positive learning environment consistent with the mission of Pacific Union College. Desirable Qualifications Master's degree in Communication, Journalism, Media Studies, Public Relations, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated ability to provide effective undergraduate instruction and support student learning. Commitment to academic excellence, student mentorship, and the mission and values of Pacific Union College. College-level teaching experience preferred. Professional experience in communication, media, journalism, public relations, or a related field preferred. Experience using instructional technology and learning management systems preferred. Compensation Hourly; Placement of the new hire within the salary pay grade is dependent on qualifications and professional teaching experience. The pay grade assigned to this position ranges from $28.27 - $37.80 hourly. Benefits: May include retirement, paid time off, and more. Full Job Description View Full Job Description Application Deadline Applications will be reviewed as received. The position will remain open until it is filled. Apply for job PACIFIC UNION COLLEGE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER. Questions? Contact Human Resources Contact Us Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Phone: (707) 965-6231 Fax: (707) 965-6400 hr@puc.edu Employee Benefits Program Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Campus Map (800) 862-7080 (707) 965-6313 Apply Give Contact Visit Careers Academics Useful Links Information Academic Departments Bookstore Calendar Campus Map Consumer Information Directory Disability Services Discrimination Policy Emergency Info Library News Online Programs Pay Student Bill Photo Gallery Privacy Policy PUC CARES Act Grant Records Office Student Planning Title IX Information For Who Are You? Current Students New Students Future Students Transfer Students Parents & Families Alumni Visitors Faculty & Staff Veterans © Copyright 2026. Pacific Union College. All Rights reserved. | Privacy policy"
