va (Republic of) Monaco Mongolia Montenegro Montserrat Morocco Mozambique Myanmar Namibia Nauru Nepal Netherlands Netherlands Antilles New Caledonia New Zealand Nicaragua Niger Nigeria Niue Norfolk Island Northern Mariana Islands Norway Oman Pakistan Palau Palestine, State of Panama Papua New Guinea Paraguay Peru Philippines Pitcairn Poland Portugal Puerto Rico Qatar Republic of Kosovo Réunion Romania Russian Federation Rwanda Saint Barthélemy Saint Helena, Ascension and Tristan da Cunha Saint Kitts and Nevis Saint Lucia Saint Martin (French part) Saint Pierre and Miquelon Saint Vincent and the Grenadines Samoa San Marino Sao Tome and Principe Saudi Arabia Senegal Serbia Seychelles Sierra Leone Singapore Sint Maarten (Dutch part) Slovakia Slovenia Solomon Islands Somalia South Africa South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands South Sudan Spain Sri Lanka Sudan Suriname Svalbard and Jan Mayen Swaziland Sweden Switzerland Syrian Arab Republic Taiwan Tajikistan Tanzania, United Republic of Thailand Timor-Leste Togo Tokelau Tonga Trinidad and Tobago Tunisia Turkey Turkmenistan Turks and Caicos Islands Tuvalu Uganda Ukraine United Arab Emirates United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland United States Minor Outlying Islands Uruguay Uzbekistan Vanuatu Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of) Viet Nam Virgin Islands (British) Virgin Islands (U.S.) Wallis and Futuna Western Sahara Yemen Zambia Zimbabwe Submit Inquiry Thank you! We'll be in touch soon. Human Resources Human Resources Human Resources Menu Academic Administration Access Services Alumni & Advancement Angwin Airport Bookstore Campus Security Campus-Services-Header.jpg Career Center Concern Discoveryland Discrimination Policy Access, Belonging and Culture Facilities Management Health Insurance Coverage Requirement Housing Human Resources Career Opportunities Faculty Job Openings Staff Job Openings Forms & Policies Information Technology Library Mail and Preferred Images Marketing & Communication Media Services Missions & Chaplain Services PUC Church Records SERVE - Survivor Empowerment, Response to Violence, and Education Service Learning Student Finance Student & Spiritual Life Student Success Center Student Wellness Center | Counseling Services Student Wellness Center | Health Services Title IX Community Recreation Contact Us Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Phone: (707) 965-6231 Fax: (707) 965-6400 hr@puc.edu Employee Benefits Program Full, Assistant, or Associate Professor of Biology Applications are available in the Human Resources Office or available online . Applications from current employees are welcome. Applicants must be members of the Seventh-day Adventist Church. Email ( hr@puc.edu ), fax (707-965-6400), or mail (Human Resources Office, One Angwin Avenue, Angwin, CA 94508), your signed application to Human Resources Please contact Human Resources regarding questions about this position. Applications from qualified applicants are forwarded to the employing department by Human Resources Applicants selected for interviews will be contacted by Human Resources or the employing department Apply for job Start Date Upon receipt of qualified applicant Job Type Faculty Job Opening Department School of Sciences Position Type Full Time Tenure Track Yes Job Summary The Full-Time Faculty Member in Biology is responsible for providing high-quality instruction in undergraduate biology and related disciplines, fostering student learning and academic success, and contributing to the mission of Pacific Union College. This position teaches assigned courses, advises and mentors students, participates in curriculum development and assessment activities, and engages in departmental, institutional, and professional service. Faculty members are expected to maintain academic expertise in their discipline, support experiential learning opportunities, and integrate faith, learning, and service consistent with the College's Seventh-day Adventist educational mission. The successful candidate collaborates with colleagues to advance student achievement, promote scientific inquiry, and contribute to a positive and academically rigorous learning environment. Desirable Qualifications Ph.D. in Biology or a related field; a background in genetics or molecular biology is preferred. Minimum of one (1) year of undergraduate teaching experience in biology or a related discipline Demonstrated ability to provide effective undergraduate instruction and support student learning. Ability to guide students conducting undergraduate research Commitment to academic excellence, student mentorship, and the mission and values of Pacific Union College. Experience advising, mentoring, or supporting students in an academic setting preferred. Experience with curriculum development, assessment, or scholarly/professional engagement preferred. Compensation Salary; Placement of the new hire within the salary pay grade is dependent on qualifications and professional teaching experience. The pay grade assigned to this position ranges from $58,797 - $78,626 annually. Benefits: May include medical, retirement, paid time off, and more. Full Job Description View Full Job Description Application Deadline Applications will be reviewed as received. The position will remain open until it is filled. Apply for job PACIFIC UNION COLLEGE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER. Questions? Contact Human Resources Contact Us Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Phone: (707) 965-6231 Fax: (707) 965-6400 hr@puc.edu Employee Benefits Program Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Campus Map (800) 862-7080 (707) 965-6313 Apply Give Contact Visit Careers Academics Useful Links Information Academic Departments Bookstore Calendar Campus Map Consumer Information Directory Disability Services Discrimination Policy Emergency Info Library News Online Programs Pay Student Bill Photo Gallery Privacy Policy PUC CARES Act Grant Records Office Student Planning Title IX Information For Who Are You? Current Students New Students Future Students Transfer Students Parents & Families Alumni Visitors Faculty & Staff Veterans © Copyright 2026. Pacific Union College. All Rights reserved. | Privacy policy"
    },
